    "text": "visual-motion here: proposed markup contract for site/index.html so styles.css/app.js can bind. Reply with your section list + any deltas; I will adapt to your ids as long as the hooks below survive.\n\nHEAD: <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"styles.css\"> (styles.css @imports tokens.css itself; do NOT link tokens.css separately), <script src=\"app.js\" defer></script>, <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">. No Google Fonts <link> — fonts are self-hosted in site/fonts/ and declared in tokens.css. <html lang=\"en\"> and add class=\"no-js\" on <html> (app.js swaps it to \"js\").\n\nBODY skeleton:\n<a class=\"skip\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a>\n<nav class=\"nav\" aria-label=\"Primary\" data-nav>\n  <a class=\"nav__mark\" href=\"#top\">Nick Salazar</a>\n  <ul class=\"nav__links\"><li><a class=\"nav__link\" href=\"#story\" data-nav-link>Story</a></li> …max 5 links, one-word labels…</ul>\n  <a class=\"nav__cta btn btn--outline btn--sm\" href=\"#contact\">Brief</a>\n  <details class=\"nav__menu\" data-nav-menu>\n    <summary class=\"nav__toggle\">Menu</summary>\n    <ul class=\"nav__sheet\"><li><a class=\"nav__link\" href=\"#story\" data-nav-link>Story</a></li> …same links…</ul>\n  </details>\n</nav>\n<main id=\"main\">\n\nHERO (is also a plate):\n<section class=\"plate plate--hero\" id=\"top\" data-plate data-hero>\n  <div class=\"plate__frame\">\n    <div class=\"plate__media\"><video class=\"plate__video\" data-video muted loop playsinline preload=\"metadata\" poster=\"assets/photos/poster-01-hero.jpg\"><source src=\"assets/videos/01-hero.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div>\n    <div class=\"plate__shade\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n    <div class=\"hero__light\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n    <div class=\"plate__copy hero__copy\">\n      <p class=\"hero__creds\" data-reveal>Second Mate Unlimited · 1600-Ton Master</p>\n      <h1 class=\"hero__name\" data-reveal><span class=\"hero__line\">Nick</span> <span class=\"hero__line\">Salazar</span></h1>\n      <p class=\"hero__role\" data-reveal>…one line…</p>\n      <a class=\"btn btn--outline hero__cta\" href=\"#contact\" data-reveal>…short label…</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\nHero video ONLY: real src attribute + preload=\"metadata\" (it is the LCP element). NO autoplay attribute on any video anywhere — app.js plays them.\n\nVIDEO PLATE (repeat ≥6; ids are your choice, used as nav anchors):\n<section class=\"plate\" id=\"coils\" data-plate>\n  <div class=\"plate__frame\">\n    <div class=\"plate__media\"><video class=\"plate__video\" data-video muted loop playsinline preload=\"none\" poster=\"assets/photos/poster-02-coils.jpg\"><source data-src=\"assets/videos/02-coils.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></div>\n    <div class=\"plate__shade\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div>\n    <div class=\"plate__copy\">\n      <h2 class=\"plate__pair\"><span class=\"plate__word\">Watch.</span> <span class=\"plate__word plate__word--accent\">Weigh.</span></h2>\n      <div class=\"plate__story\" data-reveal><p>…4–8 lines…</p></div>\n      <p class=\"plate__meta\">…caption/provenance line, optional…</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\nRules: at most ONE .plate__word--accent per plate (optionally add data-accent=\"red|yellow|sky\" on that span; default orange). Non-hero videos use data-src on <source> (lazy-attached) and preload=\"none\". Every video needs a poster. Keep .plate__frame > .plate__media, .plate__shade, .plate__copy in that DOM order (shade sits between video and copy; the copy column carries its own guaranteed backplate in CSS).\n\nTEXT SECTIONS between plates (no video):\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"services\"><div class=\"section__inner\"><h2 class=\"section__title\">…</h2><p class=\"section__lede\">…</p> …</div></section>\nServices list: <ol class=\"services\"><li class=\"services__item\" data-reveal><span class=\"services__num\" aria-hidden=\"true\">01</span><h3 class=\"services__name\">…</h3><p class=\"services__desc\">…</p></li>…</ol>\nCredentials/facts: <dl class=\"facts\"><div class=\"facts__row\"><dt>…</dt><dd>…</dd></div>…</dl>\nRunning prose: wrap in <div class=\"prose\">…</div>.\ndata-reveal goes on copy blocks you want to fade-up once (≤ ~8 per section; I stagger by DOM order). Don't put it on the nav, videos, or the form.\n\nCONTACT / ASSIGNMENT BRIEF (ids are load-bearing for app.js):\n<section class=\"section brief\" id=\"contact\"><div class=\"section__inner\">\n  <h2 class=\"section__title\">…</h2>\n  <form class=\"brief__form\" id=\"brief-form\" novalidate>\n    <div class=\"field\"><label class=\"field__label\" for=\"bf-name\">Your name</label><input class=\"input\" id=\"bf-name\" name=\"name\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"name\" aria-describedby=\"bf-name-help\"><p class=\"field__help\" id=\"bf-name-help\"></p></div>\n    same pattern for: bf-org (organisation), bf-cargo (what needs surveying), bf-where (site or port, user-entered — no coverage claim), bf-when (timing), bf-service (<select class=\"input\"> with the supplied service list), bf-notes (<textarea class=\"input input--area\">)\n    <div class=\"field\"><span class=\"field__label\">Assignment brief</span><pre class=\"brief__output\" id=\"brief-output\" tabindex=\"0\"></pre></div>\n    <div class=\"brief__actions\">\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn--fill\" id=\"brief-copy\">Copy brief</button>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"btn btn--outline\" id=\"brief-download\">Download .txt</button>\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"brief__status\" id=\"brief-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p>\n    <p class=\"brief__note\">…honest line: nothing is sent from this page; contact wiring is a pre-publication dependency…</p>\n  </form>\n</div></section>\nEvery input/select/textarea uses class=\"input\" and has an empty <p class=\"field__help\" id=\"<id>-help\"> sibling (I reserve its height). Labels above fields, always visible.\n\nFOOTER (Ft5 statement):\n<footer class=\"foot\" id=\"foot\"><p class=\"foot__line\">…one closing sentence…</p><div class=\"foot__meta\"><span class=\"foot__mark\">Nick Salazar</span><span class=\"foot__muted\">…credentials or © line…</span></div></footer>\n</main>\n\nAlso: no inline style attributes, no inline <script>, headings in order h1→h2→h3, no eyebrows/section numbers beside headings (stack vertically only). Word pairs: 2–3 words, each ≤ 10 characters so they fit at 320px. Tell me your final section ids so I can order nav highlighting.",
